1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,210
They brought three hundred men...

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:06,085
to kill one boy with a promise.

3
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:10,210
General. He isn't moving.

4
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,835
One man. Is this a joke?

5
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:17,335
They should have brought more.

6
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,710
You can't be king again, Orez!

7
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:30,585
You were king yesterday!

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,335
A king is king every day.

9
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:33,960
That's the whole point!

10
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,335
Then tell me, little king.

11
00:00:36,375 --> 00:00:39,710
What does a king do when the river floods?

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,710
He... orders it to stop?

13
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:46,210
No. He carries the first sandbag.

14
00:00:46,875 --> 00:00:50,335
Orez! Even kings fetch the water!

15
00:00:50,375 --> 00:00:51,335
Coming, Mother!

16
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,335
Mother... why do the kingdoms fight?

17
00:00:59,875 --> 00:01:03,210
Because each one believes the world is too

18
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:04,835
small to share.

19
00:01:05,375 --> 00:01:07,835
Then I'll make it one kingdom. Mine.

20
00:01:07,875 --> 00:01:10,835
And no one will be allowed to burn anything.

21
00:01:10,875 --> 00:01:11,460
Ever.

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,960
And who would follow a king so small?

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,835
Everyone. I'd ask nicely.

24
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,210
Listen to me, Orez.

25
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:22,085
A crown is not a thing you take.

26
00:01:22,125 --> 00:01:24,460
It is a thing you carry...

27
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,085
for everyone who cannot.

28
00:01:27,625 --> 00:01:28,710
Is it heavy?

29
00:01:28,875 --> 00:01:31,710
The heaviest thing in the world.

30
00:01:32,375 --> 00:01:34,585
Look! A falling star!

31
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:38,585
That is not a star!

32
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,960
Raiders! Run! Run!

33
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:47,960
Leave nothing standing.

34
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,835
Let the smoke tell Seiran whose border this is.

35
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,085
And the villagers, General?

36
00:01:56,375 --> 00:01:59,335
Smoke needs no witnesses.

37
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:03,710
Orez!

38
00:02:03,875 --> 00:02:04,710
Miki!

39
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:08,210
Don't look back. Run, Orez. Run.

40
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,210
Get up. Mother, please... get up!

41
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:18,960
We have to run.

42
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:24,460
No more running, my love. Not for me.

43
00:02:25,125 --> 00:02:28,460
Look at me. Not at the fire. At me.

44
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:33,460
Promise me... you will build that world.

45
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:37,960
The one where no child ever has to run.

46
00:02:38,625 --> 00:02:42,710
I promise. I promise! Just stay...

47
00:02:43,625 --> 00:02:45,460
My little king.

48
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:47,460
Mother?

49
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:53,960
A survivor, General. Shall I?

50
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,085
Leave him. Let him carry the story.

51
00:02:57,125 --> 00:03:00,585
Fear walks farther than my horses.

52
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:12,085
I walked until the fire was behind me.

53
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:14,335
Then I kept walking.

54
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,585
This mountain has no bread for beggars, child.

55
00:03:23,625 --> 00:03:24,960
Go home.

56
00:03:25,625 --> 00:03:26,960
I don't have one.

57
00:03:27,625 --> 00:03:29,960
Then what do you have?

58
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:31,960
A promise.

59
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,460
Promises are heavy.

60
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:40,210
Can you carry yours up these steps...

61
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:43,085
ten thousand times?

62
00:03:44,125 --> 00:03:45,210
Count them.

63
00:03:46,625 --> 00:03:48,085
Again.

64
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,460
Again.

65
00:03:51,375 --> 00:03:52,710
Again!

66
00:03:53,375 --> 00:03:56,710
A sword defeats one man.

67
00:03:56,750 --> 00:04:03,460
A mind defeats the army standing behind him.

68
00:04:04,125 --> 00:04:06,085
You left the gate open, Master.

69
00:04:06,375 --> 00:04:08,085
So I did!

70
00:04:08,625 --> 00:04:12,210
Ten thousand cuts before every dawn.

71
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:13,960
For ten winters...

72
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,710
the mountain never heard me rest.

73
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:28,335
It has no name. Out there, neither do you.

74
00:04:28,375 --> 00:04:30,585
Go and earn one.

75
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:31,710
Orez.

76
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:36,710
When you find the man who lit that fire...

77
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:38,960
what will you do?

78
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:40,835
Keep my promise.

79
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:48,210
By order of Valdhar, this town feeds the army!

80
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:50,085
Burn what is left!

81
00:04:50,375 --> 00:04:53,210
Please! Please, don't...

82
00:04:53,625 --> 00:04:55,585
Out of the way, vagrant!

83
00:04:55,875 --> 00:04:57,710
She is done running.

84
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,585
General. He isn't moving.

85
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:10,335
One man. Is this a joke?

86
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:12,085
Ten winters ago,

87
00:05:12,125 --> 00:05:15,460
you burned a village called Kiri.

88
00:05:15,875 --> 00:05:17,585
I have burned so many.

89
00:05:17,625 --> 00:05:20,960
You expect me to remember the kindling?

90
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:24,085
No. I expect you to remember me.

91
00:05:24,625 --> 00:05:26,835
Three hundred men, boy.

92
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,835
I counted. That is why I chose the bridge.

93
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:32,460
Kill him!

94
00:05:39,375 --> 00:05:42,460
Hold the line! He is one man!

95
00:06:08,875 --> 00:06:10,835
What... what are you?!

96
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,335
I'm Orez.

97
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,710
The Infinite King.

98
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,585
Then... finish it.

99
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:23,710
No. You will carry the story.

100
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:26,835
Fear walks farther than my sword.

101
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:32,835
Are they coming back?

102
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:36,460
Not here. You don't have to run anymore.

103
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:40,335
One man... took my border?!

104
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,585
The Infinite King. How ambitious. Find him.

105
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:48,710
Every king bleeds. Ready the fleet.

106
00:06:49,875 --> 00:06:52,835
Three crowns. One promise.

107
00:06:53,625 --> 00:06:55,335
Let them come.

